{"Title":"An Act relative to the exemption of the sales or use tax for leased motor vehicles","BillNumber":"H2694","DocketNumber":"HD1765","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"J_A1","Name":"James Arciero","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/J_A1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T15:37:44.26"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"J_A1","Name":"James Arciero","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/J_A1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T15:37:44.26"},{"Id":null,"Name":"Anthony M. Vacca","Type":3,"Details":null,"ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T15:58:49.3333333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H2694/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Arciero of Westford, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 2694) of James Arciero and Anthony M. Vacca relative to the exemption of the sales or use tax for leased motor vehicles.  Revenue.","DocumentText":"\tSection 6 of chapter 64H of the General Laws is hereby amended by inserting after the word “registered”, in line 353, as appearing in the 2016 Official Edition, the following words:- or leased.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J26","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J26"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}